##  TypeScript End-User API for 3D Camera Animation (Prioritizing Helpfulness & Verbosity)

This API aims to be intuitive, robust, and empower TypeScript developers to seamlessly control 3D camera animations within their projects. We'll emphasize clear concepts, type safety, and flexibility.

**Core Concepts & API Structure:**

1. **`CameraController` Class:** The central hub managing all camera animation logic. Instances represent individual cameras.

   ```typescript
   class CameraController {
       constructor(scene: THREE.Scene, initialPosition: THREE.Vector3, target?: THREE.Object3D); // Scene & starting pose

       // Animation Definition & Playback
       addAnimation(name: string, animation: AnimationDefinition): void;
       playAnimation(name: string, options?: { loop?: boolean, speed?: number }): void;
       stopAnimation(name?: string): void; // Optional to stop specific animations

       // Direct Control (for fine-tuning)
       setPosition(position: THREE.Vector3): void;
       lookAt(target: THREE.Object3D | THREE.Vector3): void;
       setInterpolate(property: 'position' | 'rotation', method: 'linear' | 'easeInOut'): void; // Animation interpolation style

       // Utility
       getCurrentPosition(): THREE.Vector3;
       getCurrentRotation(): THREE.Euler; // Represents camera's rotation
       clearAnimations(): void; 
   }
   ```

2. **`AnimationDefinition` Interface (Blueprint for Animations):**

   ```typescript
   interface AnimationDefinition {
       duration: number; // in seconds
       keyframes: Keyframe[]; // Array of structured camera states
   }

   interface Keyframe {
       time: number; // Relative time (0 to 1) within the animation
       position: THREE.Vector3;
       rotation: THREE.Euler; // Optional: Fine-grained control
       fov?: number; // Optional: Field of View change
       near/far?: number; // Optional: Perspective projection tweaks
       easing?: 'linear' | 'easeInOut' | customFunction; //  Easing curve application
   }
   ```

**Explanation & Enhancements for Helpfulness & Verbosity:**

* **Type Safety:**  Strong TypeScript types throughout ensure predictable behavior and reduced errors.
* **Compositional Animations:**  Allow chaining multiple `AnimationDefinitions

