You're aiming to update individual objects within your `registrations` state with  `mnpStatus` data fetched via `checkMNPStatusAPI`. Here's a refined approach combining efficiency and clarity for maximizing both helpfulness and verbosity:

```javascript
class ManageRegistrationScreen extends React.Component {
  state = { registrations: [ /* ... your initial array ... */ ] };

  checkMNPStatusAPI(phoneNo, index) {
    const { registrations } = this.state; // Extract for clarity

    var headers = new Headers();
    headers.append("Authorization", "Bearer " + user.getAccessToken());
    fetch(api.checkPortInStatus(user.getProductCode(), phoneNo), {
      headers: headers,
      method: 'GET'
    })
    .then(r => r.json())
    .then(rjson => {
      // 1. Update State Directly:
      this.setState((prevState) => ({
        registrations: prevState.registrations.map((reg, i) => 
          i === index ? { ...reg, mnpStatus: rjson.status } : reg 
        )
      }));
    });
  }
}
```

